WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.401
Let's bring in retired U.S.

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.570
Army Brigadier General Mark Kimmitt.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:04.404
He's the former

00:00:04.404 --> 00:00:06.573
assistant secretary of state

00:00:06.573 --> 00:00:08.875
for political and military affairs

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:11.244
under President George W Bush.

00:00:11.244 --> 00:00:11.444
All right.

00:00:11.444 --> 00:00:12.979
General Vladimir Putin

00:00:12.979 --> 00:00:16.516
is not known for putting up with a lot,

00:00:17.117 --> 00:00:18.151
especially someone

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:20.153
as belligerent as Prigozhin.

00:00:20.153 --> 00:00:22.622
So why is he tolerating this?

00:00:24.424 --> 00:00:26.226
Well, I think you've got to go back

00:00:26.226 --> 00:00:28.261
to the fall of the Soviet Union.

00:00:28.762 --> 00:00:31.765
The time between Yeltsin and Putin.

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.066
During that time,

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:35.468
the country was the wild, wild West.

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.704
And that was the rise of the oligarchs

00:00:38.004 --> 00:00:39.606
as they

00:00:39.606 --> 00:00:42.542
tried to privatize the entire industries.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.277
Industrial base

00:00:44.277 --> 00:00:45.812
inside of Russian production

00:00:45.812 --> 00:00:47.213
was one of those

00:00:47.213 --> 00:00:48.782
that took advantage of this

00:00:48.782 --> 00:00:50.483
Prigozhin is a former hotdog

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:52.685
salesman from Leningrad.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.219
But he,

00:00:53.219 --> 00:00:55.121
like so many of the other oligarchs,

00:00:55.121 --> 00:00:56.823
made billions of dollars.

00:00:56.823 --> 00:00:58.892
And candidly, when Putin came to power,

00:00:59.526 --> 00:01:01.828
there's this reciprocal relationship

00:01:01.828 --> 00:01:03.897
between the oligarchs and Putin.

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:05.565
And Prigozhin is one of them.

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:08.902
But why does

00:01:08.902 --> 00:01:11.738
he continue to put up with it now?

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:15.742
Well, first of all, he is in the debt

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:16.643
to Prigozhin,

00:01:16.643 --> 00:01:17.777
but look, let's

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.112
we've seen this in America.

00:01:19.112 --> 00:01:21.347
We've seen the rise of a nationalist

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.782
right wing

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:25.752
person who's appealing to the people

00:01:25.752 --> 00:01:26.753
on the ground

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:27.520
in many ways,

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.623
he shares the same characteristics

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:31.491
as Trump.

00:01:31.491 --> 00:01:34.060
Very, very belligerent, very, very loud,

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:37.497
goes directly to the people I think Putin

00:01:37.831 --> 00:01:39.966
no one gets a lot out of Prigozhin

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:42.035
by his mercenary army

00:01:42.035 --> 00:01:43.169
that's doing far, far

00:01:43.169 --> 00:01:45.472
better than the Russian military.

00:01:45.472 --> 00:01:46.172
And number two,

00:01:46.172 --> 00:01:47.507
I think Putin sees him

00:01:47.507 --> 00:01:49.609
as a potential political candidate

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:51.444
against him in the near future.

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:52.779
And that goes to the old saying,

00:01:52.779 --> 00:01:54.314
keep your friends close

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.682
and keep your enemies closer.

00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:57.951
That's a good explanation.

00:01:57.951 --> 00:01:59.652
Ukraine's president Zelensky,

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:00.453
of course, saying

00:02:00.453 --> 00:02:01.955
his forces are ready to begin

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.690
their counteroffensive.

00:02:03.690 --> 00:02:06.359
Have I want to take you to have a listen

00:02:06.593 --> 00:02:07.360
to what U.S.

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:09.662
National Security Adviser Jake Sullivan

00:02:09.963 --> 00:02:11.764
told our colleague Fareed

00:02:11.764 --> 00:02:15.268
Zakaria just a short time ago.

00:02:15.602 --> 00:02:16.536
Jake, when you think

00:02:16.536 --> 00:02:19.105
about the Ukrainian counteroffensive,

00:02:19.105 --> 00:02:21.541
what are you looking forward to

00:02:21.875 --> 00:02:23.943
to see that, in fact,

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.545
the massive investments

00:02:25.545 --> 00:02:26.279
the United States

00:02:26.279 --> 00:02:27.614
has made in helping

00:02:27.614 --> 00:02:30.083
Ukraine are paying off?

00:02:30.083 --> 00:02:32.252
Well, first, this is not at an exam.

00:02:32.385 --> 00:02:34.120
We're not grading Ukraine's

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.522
counteroffensive and saying,

00:02:35.522 --> 00:02:36.422
you know,

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:36.789
you did

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:38.224
well based on what we gave

00:02:38.224 --> 00:02:39.392
you, you did poorly.

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:40.193
What we want to do

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.060
is support Ukraine

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.795
to make as much progress

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.731
as possible on the battlefield.

00:02:44.731 --> 00:02:46.199
So that it is in the strongest

00:02:46.199 --> 00:02:47.233
possible position

00:02:47.233 --> 00:02:48.501
at the negotiating table.

00:02:48.501 --> 00:02:49.602
And we do believe that

00:02:49.602 --> 00:02:50.970
this counteroffensive

00:02:50.970 --> 00:02:52.172
will allow Ukraine

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.506
to take strategically

00:02:53.506 --> 00:02:55.708
significant territory back

00:02:56.042 --> 00:02:57.677
from Russia, areas

00:02:57.677 --> 00:02:58.811
occupied by Russia

00:02:58.811 --> 00:03:00.480
that are rightfully sovereign

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.714
Ukrainian territory.

00:03:04.017 --> 00:03:05.552
So does Ukraine have

00:03:05.552 --> 00:03:06.853
enough support from the U.S.

00:03:06.853 --> 00:03:07.887
and other allies

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:10.390
to succeed in a counteroffensive?

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:12.892
Well, listen, Paula,

00:03:12.892 --> 00:03:14.260
in a bit of self-promotion.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:15.662
I wrote about this

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:18.431
a month ago in The Wall Street Journal.

00:03:18.431 --> 00:03:20.433
They need to accomplish

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.901
certain milestones

00:03:21.901 --> 00:03:23.803
in this counteroffensive

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:24.971
to maintain the support

00:03:24.971 --> 00:03:25.939
of the United States

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.473
and the Western nations.

00:03:27.473 --> 00:03:29.242
They need to decisively defeat

00:03:29.242 --> 00:03:29.876
the Russians.

00:03:29.876 --> 00:03:31.911
Jake talked about that,

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.180
about making significant progress.

00:03:34.581 --> 00:03:36.749
They've got to

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:39.219
reach objectives that prepare them

00:03:39.219 --> 00:03:41.221
for further counter-offensive.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.989
So this will not be the last.

00:03:42.989 --> 00:03:45.391
They need to cut the Crimea corridor.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:47.227
They need to decisively defeat

00:03:47.227 --> 00:03:48.061
the Russians

00:03:48.061 --> 00:03:49.829
so that the Russians understand

00:03:49.829 --> 00:03:51.364
that can't win this war.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:54.000
And they need to accomplish enough

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:56.135
to keep the West onside

00:03:56.135 --> 00:03:57.804
and not seeing this as just more

00:03:57.804 --> 00:03:59.239
examples of trench warfare.

00:04:00.206 --> 00:04:00.640
So what

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:02.675
are they waiting for?

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.345
Listen, there's always a tension

00:04:05.345 --> 00:04:07.313
between the politicians and the military.

00:04:07.313 --> 00:04:08.281
The politicians

00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.450
always want this to start early.

00:04:10.917 --> 00:04:14.254
The military knows that every day

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:16.789
they the way the counter offensive,

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:17.724
they get stronger,

00:04:17.724 --> 00:04:18.992
they get more supplies,

00:04:18.992 --> 00:04:21.327
they get more intelligence on the ground.

00:04:21.327 --> 00:04:22.095
And that tension,

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:22.662
I think, is

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:23.930
what you're seeing playing out

00:04:23.930 --> 00:04:25.231
between the politicians

00:04:25.231 --> 00:04:26.099
and the commanders.

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.333
The commanders say,

00:04:27.333 --> 00:04:28.901
no, I need a couple more days

00:04:28.901 --> 00:04:30.303
to get ready.

00:04:30.370 --> 00:04:31.604
The politicians say

00:04:31.604 --> 00:04:32.972
we got to get this thing going.

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:34.841
So I think Stilinski and his generals

00:04:34.841 --> 00:04:36.342
are trying to work this out

00:04:36.342 --> 00:04:38.378
in terms of timelines.

00:04:38.378 --> 00:04:40.346
And we've seen how Russian strikes

00:04:40.346 --> 00:04:41.514
have been aimed at Kiev

00:04:41.514 --> 00:04:43.783
pretty much every day. For the last week.

00:04:43.783 --> 00:04:47.353
Is Russia trying to wear down Ukraine's

00:04:47.353 --> 00:04:48.054
air defenses?

00:04:49.589 --> 00:04:49.922
No, I

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.591
think they're trying to wear down

00:04:51.591 --> 00:04:53.026
the Ukrainian people.

00:04:53.026 --> 00:04:54.994
This is what's called a spoiling attack

00:04:54.994 --> 00:04:56.029
on the part of Russia.

00:04:56.029 --> 00:04:58.464
They know a counteroffensive is coming.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:04:59.132
So they know

00:04:59.132 --> 00:05:00.667
they can't stop the military.

00:05:00.667 --> 00:05:01.534
So they continue

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.303
to pound the civilian ends

00:05:03.303 --> 00:05:04.604
so that those civilians

00:05:04.604 --> 00:05:06.205
are the ones that say, look, let's end

00:05:06.205 --> 00:05:07.040
this thing quickly.

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:08.207
Let's get this over with.

00:05:08.207 --> 00:05:10.710
We can't take these kind of bombings.

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:12.879
But I think the Ukrainian people

00:05:12.879 --> 00:05:13.846
have demonstrated

00:05:13.846 --> 00:05:14.947
like the British people

00:05:14.947 --> 00:05:17.617
during the blitz of 1940

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:18.318
that they're willing

00:05:18.318 --> 00:05:19.786
to stand behind their military

00:05:19.786 --> 00:05:22.088
and take the attack on civilian targets.

00:05:22.355 --> 00:05:25.091
So that the military can actually conduct

00:05:25.091 --> 00:05:27.727
the offensive when and how is necessary.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:30.463
General Mark Kimmitt, thank you.

